<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarmizegetusa Regia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarmizegetusa Regia was the capital of the Dacian kingdom, built on mountain terraces at about 1,200 metres in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orastie-mountains">Orăștie Mountains</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. It had a fortress, a sacred zone of circular and rectangular sanctuaries, and workshops. Roman forces captured and destroyed it in 106 CE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>'s second Dacian War. It is part of a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarmizegetusa-regia.jpg" alt="Sarmizegetusa Regia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cosmin Stefanescu · CC BY-SA 3.0 ro · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarmisegetusa_Regia_-_Templele_patrulatere_mici_-_Zona_sacra_%E2%80%93_Gradistea_Muntelui,_Muntii_Sureanu,_Hunedoara,_Romania_19.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
